                <pb facs="0180" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/385: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-24T17:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. 1. United Christian Missionary Society plan to return two single women
                    missionaries to Batang, western Szechwan, starting about end of March. Both
                    women said to be experienced travellers and will travel with Canadian family to
                    Chengtu and from there be escorted by Chinese or Tibetan mission helpers.
                    Society requests information regarding present conditions in western China and
                    attitude of Consul General at Hankow toward assisting these women to obtain
                    necessary visas for their passports.</p>
                <p>2. After making necessary enquiries reply by naval radio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
